    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.00) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). Both benefit significantly from favorable platoon dynamics against Cavalli and Bassitt, respectively, with **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite positioning atop the order providing the highest scoring floor on the slate. **Sam Antonacci** (63.68) also warrants a strong start; despite a middling matchup, his elite 0.402 xwOBA and lead-off status make him an essential asset in our push for volume in the runs and stolen base categories.\n\nWhile we are chasing efficiency, the bench remains competitive. **Coby Mayo** (44.15) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. His score was buoyed by a friendly park factor against Cavalli, but his projected 8th-spot in the order ultimately penalized his potential for RBI and run accumulation, pushing him below the threshold set by the likes of **Liam Hicks** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** (52.77), whose scoring is suppressed by a difficult matchup against L. Gilbert (2.98 xERA). However, given our desperate need for stolen bases, his aggressive presence at the top of the order necessitates the start despite the SP skill disadvantage. Please monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and ensure no late-breaking weather alerts emerge for our high-leverage spots.",
